# JSON stays LF on every platform. A clone with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# rewrite every LF to CRLF, changing the bytes of the shipped region profiles and of
# any resume archived as JSON - files whose whole value is that they do not move.
*.json text eol=lf

# The graph record is compared byte for byte - the writer is canonical, and the tests
# check that the fixtures rewrite to themselves. A CRLF checkout would fail those tests
# on Windows only, and would hand a person a file the writer then rewrites in full.
*.ttl text eol=lf
*.trig text eol=lf
